            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0594" n="509" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg509"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.51/901a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bundy</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-12-28T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 28,
                                1918, 7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Confidential. In accordance request Liberian Government contained in last
                    paragraph your November 29, 5 p.m., Department will await receipt of full
                    written explanation, which it is assumed is now coming forward by mail.
                    Meanwhile on basis information contained in your November 29 and in accordance
                    with policy outlined in Department’s November 26 [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >29?</hi>], Department agrees with attitude of Liberian Government in
                    declining to settle matter in advance Peace Conference and settlement
                    negotiations with British and French Governments regarding refunding of loan of
                    1912.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
